sec.p:
We recruited 50 male and female volunteers from a university population. This sample size was justified by a priori precision analysis for the minimum detectable change at the 68% level (MDC68%; i.e., 1 standard deviation (SD), which is conservative in that it requires a larger sample to produce a narrow interval) for mid-thigh hypertrophy (i.e., \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
